WEBVTT

00:13.620 --> 00:14.920
You awake?

00:17.640 --> 00:20.950
Roddy here found you passed out.

00:21.800 --> 00:26.460
Getting you back here and in bed
 all by myself was a ton of work, y'know?

00:38.860 --> 00:42.350
Is this what you're worried about?

00:43.130 --> 00:44.230
My card—

00:46.500 --> 00:51.110
You're freezing, boy.
Your body temperature is way too low.

00:51.560 --> 00:53.110
You should stay in bed.

00:56.520 --> 00:58.340
You work for Theodore, don't you?

00:59.120 --> 01:02.370
You reek of it.

01:03.420 --> 01:05.420
I can tell, you know?

01:06.270 --> 01:08.460
My nose is better than his.

01:10.330 --> 01:12.570
Who are you?

01:13.330 --> 01:18.890
"What you need is manners, grace, 
and a readiness to risk your life."

01:19.410 --> 01:21.010
I'm a High Card.

01:27.170 --> 01:29.810
I am so blind

01:29.810 --> 01:31.810
Still running

01:32.090 --> 01:35.030
Running out of sight

01:35.030 --> 01:36.680
In the night

01:36.680 --> 01:39.190
I'm feeling goosebumps

01:40.560 --> 01:47.660
Betting against the odds again,
I'm being swayed like in a dance

01:47.660 --> 01:52.330
No more Blah Blah Bluff-filled Table

01:53.940 --> 01:55.820
Just tell me how to figure it out

01:55.820 --> 01:57.630
Inside my head, I'm painting the town

01:57.630 --> 01:58.840
Addition is affliction

01:58.840 --> 01:59.710
Something's missing

01:59.710 --> 02:01.530
(Oh you really got me wrong)

02:01.530 --> 02:03.390
I wanna get out so I'm taking a chance

02:03.390 --> 02:04.250
I gotta advance

02:04.250 --> 02:05.440
You know who I am?

02:05.440 --> 02:06.890
I'm a trickster

02:07.760 --> 02:09.350
Just take a chance

02:09.350 --> 02:10.520
Play the game

02:10.520 --> 02:12.520
It sounds insane

02:12.520 --> 02:15.690
Fate smiles at the borderline

02:15.690 --> 02:22.030
Rather than dance to someone else's tune,
I wanna dance to my own.

02:22.030 --> 02:23.990
Yea I'm moving like that

02:23.990 --> 02:25.290
Give it a try

02:25.290 --> 02:26.410
Keep on going down

02:26.410 --> 02:29.090
I just need something real

02:29.090 --> 02:32.660
Then we need no fakes

02:32.660 --> 02:36.920
I'll let my soul be wild and free

03:05.650 --> 03:10.410
This is the sleeper train 
Chris and Finn were aboard.

03:10.650 --> 03:15.540
It's approximately 25 kilometers north
 of the station where they were to disembark.

03:15.870 --> 03:19.660
It seems they encountered another player.

03:20.200 --> 03:21.620
Any word from them?

03:21.930 --> 03:23.780
Not yet, I'm afraid.

03:23.780 --> 03:26.930
I believe it's safe to say they've 
met with some sort of trouble.

03:26.930 --> 03:28.750
We should go to Polostick after them!

03:28.750 --> 03:29.440
I agree.

03:29.440 --> 03:30.320
No.

03:30.320 --> 03:34.920
Master Theodore has ordered 
High Card to be on standby.

03:34.920 --> 03:38.360
But Chris and Finn might 
be waiting for our rescue.

03:38.360 --> 03:40.120
We're a team, aren't we?

03:43.030 --> 03:44.140
Leo!

03:45.630 --> 03:50.040
No matter what happens, 
orders must be followed.

03:52.270 --> 03:56.040
Your suit was tailor-made 
by Wizardsman, I see.

03:57.100 --> 03:59.460
Old Maid Street, huh?

04:04.810 --> 04:06.180
Now then...

04:06.550 --> 04:11.740
you came to steal my card,
yet I ended up saving you.

04:11.740 --> 04:14.190
You're a silly player, aren't you?

04:15.240 --> 04:18.820
What did you mean when
 you said you're a High Card?

04:20.170 --> 04:22.090
It's ancient history.

04:22.790 --> 04:24.840
So there were others before us?

04:24.840 --> 04:26.070
"Us"?

04:27.000 --> 04:28.450
I'm also a High Card.

04:30.580 --> 04:31.710
That's right...

04:32.060 --> 04:34.330
Do you know what happened to the train?

04:34.330 --> 04:35.580
Was there an accident?

04:36.450 --> 04:39.840
<i>More on the sleeper train that made 
an emergency stop early this morning.</i>

04:40.150 --> 04:42.970
<i>They've found fallen rocks across the rails</i>

04:42.970 --> 04:45.110
<i>just meters ahead of the stopped train.</i>

04:45.110 --> 04:49.140
<i>What exactly led up to the 
emergency stop remains unclear,</i>

04:49.140 --> 04:51.850
<i>and investigation is ongoing.</i>

04:52.330 --> 04:54.240
I was on that train.

04:54.240 --> 04:58.820
Guys from the Klondike Family 
attacked us after being tipped off.

05:01.260 --> 05:02.430
And Chris...

05:02.430 --> 05:03.610
Chris?

05:04.130 --> 05:06.330
My colleague from High Card.

05:06.890 --> 05:08.870
He was on the train with me.

05:09.750 --> 05:11.810
Chris from High Card...

05:13.170 --> 05:17.120
Would that happen to be Chris Redgrave?

05:17.120 --> 05:18.890
Er, yeah, that's him.

05:19.240 --> 05:20.420
You're kidding...

05:21.110 --> 05:22.530
My goodness.

05:25.930 --> 05:26.950
Chris—

05:35.830 --> 05:38.360
Come on, come on, <i>come on</i>!
 What is this?!

05:38.360 --> 05:39.900
What the hell?!

05:39.900 --> 05:42.150
Where's the card?!

05:42.150 --> 05:43.220
Damn it!

05:44.130 --> 05:46.350
Are you sure you searched everywhere?

05:46.350 --> 05:48.320
You should try being more thorough.

05:48.970 --> 05:50.860
I already did that!

05:50.860 --> 05:52.430
Where is it? Where's the card?!

05:52.430 --> 05:53.470
Tell me!

05:53.470 --> 05:54.200
Spill it!

05:56.220 --> 05:58.080
I forgot.

06:01.780 --> 06:05.060
You're making a fool of me, aren't you?

06:05.620 --> 06:08.820
You have been all this time, huh?

06:09.390 --> 06:10.970
Well, not anymore.

06:11.640 --> 06:16.040
I'll be thorough, all right.
So get ready for a thorough thrashing.

06:18.670 --> 06:22.190
Now... where's the card?!

06:49.900 --> 06:51.010
Eat up.

06:51.010 --> 06:52.590
Thank you.

06:53.170 --> 06:54.260
But why go out of your way?

06:54.580 --> 06:57.230
Aren't I a nice gal?

06:59.170 --> 07:00.760
It's only natural, you know?

07:03.170 --> 07:07.190
I happened upon you passed out,
 so I carried you here.

07:07.810 --> 07:10.210
Your clothes were soaked, so I dried them.

07:10.520 --> 07:13.220
You were injured, so I patched you up.

07:13.650 --> 07:15.080
That's just how it goes.

07:16.390 --> 07:21.900
Besides, I'm sick and tired
of folks dying in front of me.

07:22.870 --> 07:25.460
Even if they're after my life.

07:30.770 --> 07:33.460
Hey, what are you doing?

07:33.460 --> 07:38.450
Get eating while it's still hot. 
Warm yourself up from the inside.

07:38.970 --> 07:39.990
Come on.

07:42.330 --> 07:44.860
You wanna go rescue Chris, don't you?

07:49.190 --> 07:52.210
Jeez. You're a handful, aren't you?

07:53.460 --> 07:56.790
You said you were sick and tired
 of seeing people die...

07:57.500 --> 08:00.540
Did something happen with High Card?

08:02.140 --> 08:04.880
You sound like you know Chris, too.

08:08.700 --> 08:11.250
You show up here.

08:12.040 --> 08:14.040
You're a High Card.

08:14.970 --> 08:17.900
And you're curious about my past.

08:19.000 --> 08:22.130
This could naturally all be a coincidence.

08:22.500 --> 08:24.820
But there must be meaning behind it.

08:25.480 --> 08:27.020
That's what I want to believe.

08:29.790 --> 08:31.630
It's a boring story.

08:35.640 --> 08:39.900
When I first started working 
as part of High Card...

08:40.970 --> 08:46.290
Let's see... It was about 25 years ago now.

08:52.370 --> 08:54.340
I just kind of enjoyed it.

08:54.710 --> 08:57.220
I felt like I'd become a hero.

08:59.130 --> 09:01.510
I saw my share of danger.

09:03.230 --> 09:06.010
I'd get dragged into fights too.

09:08.140 --> 09:12.190
I was in love with my work 
as a member of High Card.

09:15.720 --> 09:17.270
It was my life.

09:18.870 --> 09:25.210
But... the trigger was the death of 
a colleague, who was a messenger.

09:27.900 --> 09:29.290
What are you doing?

09:29.290 --> 09:31.150
Find the player who escaped.

09:32.010 --> 09:33.180
Get going.

09:34.810 --> 09:36.690
I want to stay by his side.

09:37.330 --> 09:39.720
Collecting the cards is our top priority.

09:51.970 --> 09:55.240
Once my mind was seized by 
a certain thought, I couldn't shake it.

09:56.360 --> 09:59.740
The emotions I tried 
to ignore started to overflow.

10:00.750 --> 10:03.260
After more than ten years with High Card,

10:03.260 --> 10:06.380
they'd accumulated like dregs 
at the bottom of my heart.

10:07.290 --> 10:12.650
I had questions about the way Theodore 
did business and suspicions about Pinochle.

10:14.120 --> 10:15.230
And then...

10:17.050 --> 10:19.170
something decisive happened.

10:32.820 --> 10:35.030
Tyler, how's the kid?

10:36.360 --> 10:37.430
Tyler...

10:39.230 --> 10:43.310
If I use X-Hand with my cards,
 I can save Chris.

10:44.140 --> 10:47.410
We have to. It's the only way.

10:47.410 --> 10:48.660
I can't allow that.

10:49.060 --> 10:50.510
Theodore!

10:50.510 --> 10:54.180
The king prohibits the playing 
of cards for personal use.

10:54.810 --> 10:57.670
No one is allowed to break that rule.

10:58.550 --> 11:00.930
Especially not members of High Card.

11:01.500 --> 11:03.800
I'm sure you know this already.

11:03.800 --> 11:06.430
And X-Hand is out of question.

11:06.670 --> 11:09.810
Please, I have to save my son!

11:09.810 --> 11:12.310
Aya, collect his card.

11:16.090 --> 11:20.690
But... this is the only way to save my boy.

11:20.690 --> 11:23.780
Please, I'm begging you 
to look the other way.

11:24.570 --> 11:26.080
I don't want my son to die.

11:26.550 --> 11:29.710
You're a father too, so you must understand.

11:30.490 --> 11:32.080
Come on, Theodore.

11:34.020 --> 11:36.940
Please... I'm begging you.

11:37.960 --> 11:39.720
Chris is going to die!

11:43.970 --> 11:45.170
It's fate.

11:46.770 --> 11:47.600
Aya.

11:54.090 --> 11:58.110
I'll right this wrong with my own hands.

12:05.120 --> 12:06.740
D-Don't do it!

12:11.150 --> 12:14.390
You're the one who's wrong, Theodore!

12:14.390 --> 12:16.090
Tyler! Now's your chance!

12:16.090 --> 12:17.420
Don't you dare, Tyler!

12:24.860 --> 12:27.050
Play! X-Hand!

12:31.940 --> 12:33.650
Tyler!

12:59.980 --> 13:07.090
Tyler played a hand of four cards to save
 his son... at the cost of his own life.

13:08.990 --> 13:14.990
I became disenchanted with everything
and lost sight of who I was.

13:15.610 --> 13:20.470
I left High Card without telling anyone 
and wandered the nation.

13:28.110 --> 13:34.550
Eventually, I found my 
way here and settled in.

13:39.310 --> 13:41.150
With this fella.

13:43.470 --> 13:47.090
Back then, I thought I was in the right.

13:47.790 --> 13:49.950
I was sure Theodore was wrong.

13:51.230 --> 13:54.770
But as a result, Tyler died.

14:02.100 --> 14:07.610
With X-Hand, the bigger a hand is,
 the stronger it becomes.

14:07.610 --> 14:12.120
And the bigger the hand is,
 the greater the toll on the player.

14:12.570 --> 14:16.900
Playing four cards killed Tyler.

14:19.970 --> 14:24.540
If Tyler hadn't used X-Hand, 
he'd still be alive.

14:25.300 --> 14:28.060
But then, Chris would have...

14:29.260 --> 14:31.540
I don't regret what I did.

14:32.260 --> 14:41.520
But looking back, I'm not sure 
whether I or Theodore was right.

14:51.320 --> 14:52.900
The jack of clubs...

14:53.350 --> 14:55.790
Aya Tawawa's card has yet to be collected.

14:55.790 --> 14:56.780
Sir.

14:57.160 --> 15:01.790
The Klondikes intercepted 
the train bound for Polostick.

15:02.210 --> 15:06.440
We've lost contact with Chris and Finn, 
who were en route to collect it.

15:07.670 --> 15:08.800
I'm worried.

15:09.710 --> 15:11.610
Get on with it.

15:14.290 --> 15:14.940
Sir.

15:15.930 --> 15:19.560
For a jokester, you're made
 of pretty tough stuff, huh?

15:19.970 --> 15:22.340
Man, I've had enough of this.

15:22.340 --> 15:24.940
Just fess up and tell me where the card is.

15:25.280 --> 15:27.200
Come on. Tell me.

15:28.120 --> 15:29.380
Wh-Where did...

15:29.380 --> 15:30.100
Huh?

15:31.010 --> 15:33.550
...the other one go?

15:34.290 --> 15:35.870
You mean Alex?

15:35.870 --> 15:38.700
He's looking for your partner 
who fell in the river.

15:39.310 --> 15:42.330
We're trying to move up in the family,

15:42.880 --> 15:45.590
so he won't be letting your friend get away.

15:45.590 --> 15:48.630
We'll take his card...

15:49.860 --> 15:52.520
even if it's off his dead body!

15:56.920 --> 15:58.520
How are you feeling?

15:58.520 --> 16:01.620
All better. I can move now.

16:01.620 --> 16:02.350
Thank you.

16:05.250 --> 16:07.160
Aren't I a nice gal?

16:11.490 --> 16:17.210
Theodore has left me alone for over a decade.

16:17.850 --> 16:23.120
And now he sends a new 
High Card to collect my card.

16:23.540 --> 16:26.330
Just as the next king-to-be is assassinated,

16:26.680 --> 16:32.300
the capital is under martial law, 
and the whole nation is in crisis.

16:32.850 --> 16:33.710
Aya...

16:34.340 --> 16:35.850
I know.

16:43.960 --> 16:48.980
If you were in my shoes, 
what would you have done?

16:52.930 --> 16:58.190
I joined High Card because 
I wanted to save Sun Fields.

16:58.990 --> 17:02.690
I collect cards because it's my job.

17:03.480 --> 17:06.750
I don't have any sort 
of guiding belief or ideals.

17:07.530 --> 17:10.980
But if something like that happened to me...

17:13.790 --> 17:15.630
I'd work my ass off!

17:26.270 --> 17:28.050
I like you.

17:29.630 --> 17:31.530
I said what I had to say.

17:31.880 --> 17:34.150
I trust you to draw 
your own conclusions, boy...

17:35.130 --> 17:40.160
Finn Oldman of High Card.

17:53.420 --> 17:54.910
There you are.

18:05.830 --> 18:07.100
A player!

18:07.570 --> 18:09.790
Roddy, you go and hide.

18:09.790 --> 18:11.230
Finn! My card!

18:14.550 --> 18:15.460
Play!

18:21.490 --> 18:23.080
"Coming Home"!

18:23.740 --> 18:25.400
Whoa!

18:26.280 --> 18:31.380
"Coming Home" lets me pull anything
 in my field of vision toward me.

18:52.380 --> 18:53.770
Incredible...

18:57.000 --> 18:58.440
Oh, boy.

18:58.810 --> 19:01.270
I haven't run like that in years.

19:12.060 --> 19:14.290
One more card...

19:14.550 --> 19:18.050
Jeez, this is so tiring.

19:22.420 --> 19:26.060
Tch, he moved to an open area...

19:39.320 --> 19:41.320
Damn it! What gives?!

19:54.910 --> 19:56.020
Roddy!

20:44.040 --> 20:45.580
Chris!

20:46.190 --> 20:47.700
I'm glad you are okay!

20:49.670 --> 20:52.170
That wound... Aren't you going to heal it?

20:57.950 --> 20:58.760
Here.

20:59.210 --> 20:59.860
Thanks.

21:02.190 --> 21:03.990
Is that boy Chris?

21:07.860 --> 21:09.100
With this...

21:10.900 --> 21:12.120
Hey!

21:12.550 --> 21:15.330
I've collected Aya's card according to plan.

21:15.330 --> 21:17.210
You get the other player's?

21:24.010 --> 21:25.330
Knock that off!

21:25.330 --> 21:26.750
We collected the card.

21:26.750 --> 21:27.890
Our mission's complete.

21:30.520 --> 21:31.380
Chris?

21:32.380 --> 21:34.660
I didn't want you to know.

21:36.410 --> 21:37.980
I'm sorry, Finn.

22:05.070 --> 22:09.280
We move on, kicking away a crisis

22:09.280 --> 22:16.700
Dare to cause a dramatic upset

22:18.650 --> 22:23.410
To those of you in the safe zone
who hate to rock the boat

22:23.410 --> 22:26.850
Over here, I'm barely surviving today

22:26.850 --> 22:29.160
In exchange for my MP

22:29.160 --> 22:32.740
I can't cool down this burning passion

22:32.740 --> 22:36.710
Bring it, weak-ass monsters!

22:36.710 --> 22:40.180
With that said, my knees are shaking

22:40.180 --> 22:42.770
But I still dream on

22:42.770 --> 22:46.840
Because I don't want to make myself a liar

22:46.840 --> 22:50.690
(Are you all ready?)

22:49.450 --> 22:51.540
And don't be afraid

22:51.540 --> 22:53.390
Let's get sassy

22:53.390 --> 22:56.680
I'm sharpening the senses I lost

22:56.680 --> 23:00.700
Repeating a desperate act to get in the zone

23:01.610 --> 23:05.910
We move on, welcoming any phenomenon

23:05.910 --> 23:12.100
I challenge myself on the lifeline I run on

23:12.100 --> 23:15.660
Please let it slide if I take a huge tumble

23:15.660 --> 23:20.580
I smile as I go, dedicating my whole life

23:20.580 --> 23:23.420
That's why I get serious

23:23.420 --> 23:25.670
So I can leave my tracks

23:25.670 --> 23:31.890
Shake up the destiny in my hand

23:36.570 --> 23:39.250
Next time: "CHRIS."
